e. As he poured over the yellowed pages of a forgotten thesis, Matt's mind began to wander back to the vibrant streets of Berlin, where the sounds of punk rock and Turkish delight vendors had provided the soundtrack to their formative years. He recalled the countless nights spent exploring the city's underground art scene, where the avant-garde and the anarchic had blended seamlessly with the academic and the intellectual. The memories came flooding back, and Matt's fingers instinctively reached for the worn leather journal he had kept during those tumultuous years. The creased pages, filled with scribbled notes, doodles, and cryptic quotes, seemed to hold the essence of his time at the Free University Berlin. As he flipped through the journal, a faded ticket stub from a Fugazi concert at the Kreuzberg's iconic SO36 club slipped out, carrying with it the whispers of a bygone era. In this moment, surrounded by the musty relics of academia, Matt Oliver was transported back to a time when the world had seemed full of possibilities, and the boundaries between theory and practice had blurred into a vibrant, messy, and beautiful whole.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the 